# Scenario A4 – Banking App: Replica Set

Replica set name: `rs0`  
Members: `localhost:27017`, `localhost:27018`, `localhost:27019`  
Database: `bankDB`  
Collection: `accounts`

## Step 1 – Create data folders

Open Command Prompt and run:

```cmd
cd /d C:\
mkdir data
mkdir data\rs0-1
mkdir data\rs0-2
mkdir data\rs0-3
```

If a folder already exists, Windows may print a message; that is okay.

## Step 2 – Start the three MongoDB servers

Open **three separate Command Prompt windows**. Run one command in each window and leave all three windows open:

Window 1:

```cmd
mongod --replSet rs0 --port 27017 --dbpath C:\data\rs0-1 --bind_ip localhost
```

Window 2:

```cmd
mongod --replSet rs0 --port 27018 --dbpath C:\data\rs0-2 --bind_ip localhost
```

Window 3:

```cmd
mongod --replSet rs0 --port 27019 --dbpath C:\data\rs0-3 --bind_ip localhost
```

You can also double-click the corresponding `.bat` files in this folder.

## Step 3 – Initiate the replica set

Open a fourth Command Prompt window:

```cmd
mongosh --host localhost --port 27017
```

At the `mongosh` prompt, run:

```javascript
load("C:/path/to/mongodb-practical-github/scenario-a4-banking-replica-set/05-initiate-replica-set.js")
```

Wait for the replica set election to finish. Check it using:

```javascript
rs.status()
```


Open another CMD window:

```cmd
mongosh "mongodb://localhost:27017,localhost:27018,localhost:27019/bankDB?replicaSet=rs0"
```

Run the numbered `.js` files with `load("C:/full/path/file.js")`, or copy their contents into `mongosh`.




